𝗧𝗲𝗿𝗿𝗮𝗳𝗼𝗿𝗺 𝗧𝗶𝗽: 𝗡𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗱 𝗠𝗮𝗽𝘀 + 𝗳𝗼𝗿_𝗲𝗮𝗰𝗵 𝗦𝗶𝗺𝗽𝗹𝗶𝗳𝗶𝗲𝗱! 🌟

📌 𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝗶𝘀 𝗮 𝗡𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗱 𝗠𝗮𝗽?
A 𝗻𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗱 𝗺𝗮𝗽 in Terraform is simply a map within another map. It’s super handy for managing structured data like multiple environments or grouped resources — all in a clean, organized way.

🧩 𝗕𝗮𝘀𝗶𝗰 𝗦𝘆𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘅:
variable "example" {
  type = map(map(string))
  default = {
    dev = {
      app = "app-dev"
      db  = "db-dev"
    }
  prod = {
     app = "app-prod"
     db  = "db-prod"
  }
 }
}
Here, example is a map containing other maps for each environment.

⚙️ 𝗪𝗵𝘆 𝘂𝘀𝗲 𝗡𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗱 𝗠𝗮𝗽 + 𝗳𝗼𝗿_𝗲𝗮𝗰𝗵?
One common problem with plain map + for_each is handling 𝗺𝘂𝗹𝘁𝗶𝗽𝗹𝗲 𝗻𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗱 𝘀𝗲𝘁𝘀 𝗼𝗳 𝗿𝗲𝘀𝗼𝘂𝗿𝗰𝗲𝘀. For example, deploying VMs or resource groups across different environments.

